<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The demo plant's machine model (docs/demo/spec.md *The machines' signals*), loaded by the five demo PLCs
  (apps/OpcServer/emulator/config/demo, /emulator/plc/nodeset) and by nothing else:  one MachineType, and one Machine of it under
  Objects with its five variables declared under it, since NodeSet2 instantiates no type.  Every PLC loads this one file, so a
  node's id is the same on all five and one hub template over Machine resolves on each.
    status       Boolean, true while the machine runs:  OEE's State.
    totalCount   UInt32, the units made:  OEE's Total.
    rejectCount  UInt32, the units rejected:  OEE's Reject.  A machine with no reject share has no tag for it and reads this file's 0.
    reasonCode   Int32, the stop's reason code, 0 for none:  OEE's Reason.
    speed        Double, in units a minute, an AnalogItem whose EURange is 0 to 100 - the filler's 60 a minute is the plant's ceiling.
  Every variable is AccessLevel 1, CurrentRead alone.  The emulator writes its own nodes inside the server, which the attribute does
  not stop (open62541's admin session has every right), and no session can write one, a visitor's through the node browser included,
  whatever the server's access callback would allow:  the counts, the status and the code are the emulator's alone.  No history
  here:  the PLC keeps none, the hub's historian does.
-->
